{
  "info": {
    "name": "Crucible v1",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "PayPal SANDBOX flow + Crucible API. Secrets come from the environment only (fill PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID / PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET in the 'Crucible sandbox' environment; never commit them). Never point paypal_base_url at a live host."
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "PayPal Sandbox",
      "description": "SANDBOX ONLY. Setup: in the 'Crucible sandbox' environment fill PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID and PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET (sandbox REST app credentials; never commit them, never use live credentials). Run in order: OAuth token, Create order, Create order (replay), Get order, then approve the order as the sandbox BUYER (open the `paypal_approval_url` variable in a browser, log in with the sandbox personal account, approve; or run `scripts/paypal_live_check.py`, which automates this through Kernel). Then Approval-state check, Capture, Capture replay, Duplicate capture, Final check. Creating an order is never approval, and approval is never capture. Capture requests are sent to a real order only when the order status is APPROVED.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. OAuth token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{paypal_base_url}}/v1/oauth2/token"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "grant_type=client_credentials"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID}}",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Sandbox only: refuse to send anything to a non-sandbox PayPal host.",
                  "if (pm.environment.get('paypal_base_url') !== 'https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com') throw new Error('paypal_base_url must be the sandbox host');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('bearer', () => pm.expect(j.token_type).to.eql('Bearer'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('paypal_access_token', j.access_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Create order ($1.00 USD, intent CAPTURE)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "PayPal-Request-Id",
                "value": "{{paypal_create_request_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{paypal_base_url}}/v2/checkout/orders"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"intent\": \"CAPTURE\",\n  \"purchase_units\": [\n    {\n      \"custom_id\": \"postman-{{paypal_create_request_id}}\",\n      \"amount\": {\n        \"currency_code\": \"USD\",\n        \"value\": \"1.00\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"payment_source\": {\n    \"paypal\": {\n      \"experience_context\": {\n        \"user_action\": \"PAY_NOW\",\n        \"shipping_preference\": \"NO_SHIPPING\",\n        \"return_url\": \"https://example.com/return\",\n        \"cancel_url\": \"https://example.com/cancel\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{paypal_access_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Sandbox only: refuse to send anything to a non-sandbox PayPal host.",
                  "if (pm.environment.get('paypal_base_url') !== 'https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com') throw new Error('paypal_base_url must be the sandbox host');",
                  "pm.environment.set('paypal_create_request_id', 'postman-' + pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$guid}}'));  // one stable id per order; step 3 replays it"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('created', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200,201]));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('exact amount', () => pm.expect(j.purchase_units[0].amount.value).to.eql('1.00'));",
                  "pm.test('not approved yet', () => pm.expect(['CREATED','PAYER_ACTION_REQUIRED']).to.include(j.status));",
                  "const link = (j.links || []).find(l => l.rel === 'payer-action' || l.rel === 'approve');",
                  "pm.test('approval link present', () => pm.expect(link).to.be.ok);",
                  "pm.environment.set('paypal_order_id', j.id);",
                  "pm.environment.set('paypal_order_status', j.status);",
                  "if (link) pm.environment.set('paypal_approval_url', link.href);  // secret-grade: open it as the sandbox buyer, do not share"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Create order (idempotent replay, same PayPal-Request-Id)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "PayPal-Request-Id",
                "value": "{{paypal_create_request_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{paypal_base_url}}/v2/checkout/orders"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"intent\": \"CAPTURE\",\n  \"purchase_units\": [\n    {\n      \"custom_id\": \"postman-{{paypal_create_request_id}}\",\n      \"amount\": {\n        \"currency_code\": \"USD\",\n        \"value\": \"1.00\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"payment_source\": {\n    \"paypal\": {\n      \"experience_context\": {\n        \"user_action\": \"PAY_NOW\",\n        \"shipping_preference\": \"NO_SHIPPING\",\n        \"return_url\": \"https://example.com/return\",\n        \"cancel_url\": \"https://example.com/cancel\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{paypal_access_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Sandbox only: refuse to send anything to a non-sandbox PayPal host.",
                  "if (pm.environment.get('paypal_base_url') !== 'https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com') throw new Error('paypal_base_url must be the sandbox host');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('replay ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200,201]));",
                  "pm.test('same order, not a second one', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.eql(pm.environment.get('paypal_order_id')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Get order",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{paypal_base_url}}/v2/checkout/orders/{{paypal_order_id}}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{paypal_access_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Sandbox only: refuse to send anything to a non-sandbox PayPal host.",
                  "if (pm.environment.get('paypal_base_url') !== 'https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com') throw new Error('paypal_base_url must be the sandbox host');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const s = pm.response.json().status;",
                  "pm.test('known status', () => pm.expect(['CREATED','PAYER_ACTION_REQUIRED','APPROVED','COMPLETED']).to.include(s));",
                  "pm.environment.set('paypal_order_status', s);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Capture BEFORE approval (expected failure)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "PayPal-Request-Id",
                "value": "early-{{paypal_order_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{paypal_base_url}}/v2/checkout/orders/{{paypal_capture_probe_id}}/capture"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{paypal_access_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected failure example: a capture without buyer approval is rejected (422 ORDER_NOT_APPROVED / PAYER_ACTION_REQUIRED)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Sandbox only: refuse to send anything to a non-sandbox PayPal host.",
                  "if (pm.environment.get('paypal_base_url') !== 'https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com') throw new Error('paypal_base_url must be the sandbox host');",
                  "// Safety: if the order is already approved this request is pointed at a bogus id (404) so it can never capture.",
                  "const s = pm.environment.get('paypal_order_status');",
                  "pm.environment.set('paypal_capture_probe_id', (s === 'APPROVED' || s === 'COMPLETED') ? 'NOT-AN-ORDER' : pm.environment.get('paypal_order_id'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "const issue = ((j.details || [])[0] || {}).issue;",
                  "pm.test('rejected, nothing captured', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([422, 404]));",
                  "pm.test('typed reason', () => pm.expect(['ORDER_NOT_APPROVED','PAYER_ACTION_REQUIRED','RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND','INVALID_RESOURCE_ID']).to.include(issue || j.name));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Approval-state check (approve as the sandbox buyer first)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{paypal_base_url}}/v2/checkout/orders/{{paypal_order_id}}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{paypal_access_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Sandbox only: refuse to send anything to a non-sandbox PayPal host.",
                  "if (pm.environment.get('paypal_base_url') !== 'https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com') throw new Error('paypal_base_url must be the sandbox host');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const s = pm.response.json().status;",
                  "pm.environment.set('paypal_order_status', s);",
                  "pm.test('order readable', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('buyer has approved (status APPROVED)', () => pm.expect(s).to.eql('APPROVED'));  // fails until the buyer approves"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "7. Capture order (only sent once APPROVED)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "PayPal-Request-Id",
                "value": "capture-{{paypal_order_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{paypal_base_url}}/v2/checkout/orders/{{paypal_capture_target}}/capture"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{paypal_access_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Sandbox only: refuse to send anything to a non-sandbox PayPal host.",
                  "if (pm.environment.get('paypal_base_url') !== 'https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com') throw new Error('paypal_base_url must be the sandbox host');",
                  "// Run step 6 first. Not APPROVED => this goes to a bogus id and fails harmlessly with 404.",
                  "pm.environment.set('paypal_capture_target', pm.environment.get('paypal_order_status') === 'APPROVED' ? pm.environment.get('paypal_order_id') : 'RUN-STEP-6-FIRST');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('captured', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200,201]));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "const c = j.purchase_units[0].payments.captures[0];",
                  "pm.test('COMPLETED', () => pm.expect(c.status).to.eql('COMPLETED'));",
                  "pm.test('exact amount', () => pm.expect([c.amount.value, c.amount.currency_code]).to.eql(['1.00','USD']));",
                  "pm.environment.set('paypal_capture_id', c.id);",
                  "pm.environment.set('paypal_order_status', j.status);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "8. Capture replay (same PayPal-Request-Id: no second charge)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "PayPal-Request-Id",
                "value": "capture-{{paypal_order_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{paypal_base_url}}/v2/checkout/orders/{{paypal_order_id}}/capture"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{paypal_access_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Sandbox only: refuse to send anything to a non-sandbox PayPal host.",
                  "if (pm.environment.get('paypal_base_url') !== 'https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com') throw new Error('paypal_base_url must be the sandbox host');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('replay ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200,201]));",
                  "pm.test('same capture id', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().purchase_units[0].payments.captures[0].id).to.eql(pm.environment.get('paypal_capture_id')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "9. Duplicate capture (NEW request id: expected failure)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "PayPal-Request-Id",
                "value": "dup-{{paypal_order_id}}-{{$guid}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{paypal_base_url}}/v2/checkout/orders/{{paypal_dup_target}}/capture"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{paypal_access_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Sandbox only: refuse to send anything to a non-sandbox PayPal host.",
                  "if (pm.environment.get('paypal_base_url') !== 'https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com') throw new Error('paypal_base_url must be the sandbox host');",
                  "// Only meaningful after step 7. Before that it must not run against an approved-but-uncaptured order.",
                  "pm.environment.set('paypal_dup_target', pm.environment.get('paypal_capture_id') ? pm.environment.get('paypal_order_id') : 'RUN-STEP-7-FIRST');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('second capture refused', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test('ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED', () => pm.expect(((pm.response.json().details || [])[0] || {}).issue).to.eql('ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "10. Final check: exactly one capture",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{paypal_base_url}}/v2/checkout/orders/{{paypal_order_id}}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{paypal_access_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Sandbox only: refuse to send anything to a non-sandbox PayPal host.",
                  "if (pm.environment.get('paypal_base_url') !== 'https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com') throw new Error('paypal_base_url must be the sandbox host');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('COMPLETED', () => pm.expect(j.status).to.eql('COMPLETED'));",
                  "pm.test('exactly one capture', () => pm.expect(j.purchase_units[0].payments.captures.length).to.eql(1));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Crucible API",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base_url}}/health"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('ok'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Provider status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base_url}}/providers/status"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('bestbuy disabled', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().providers.bestbuy.enabled).to.eql(false));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Catalog search",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base_url}}/catalog/search?q=running shoes&max_price=100"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('source + as_of stamped', () => { pm.expect(j.source).to.be.a('string'); pm.expect(j).to.have.property('snapshot'); });",
                  "pm.test('budget respected', () => j.products.forEach(p => pm.expect(parseFloat(p.price)).to.be.at.most(100)));",
                  "if (j.products.length) pm.environment.set('product_id', j.products[0].id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Product detail",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base_url}}/catalog/products/{{product_id}}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 or 404', () => pm.expect([200,404]).to.include(pm.response.code));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Product reviews",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base_url}}/catalog/products/{{product_id}}/reviews?focus=durability&limit=5"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('has availability flag', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property('reviews_available'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Propose purchase",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base_url}}/purchase/propose"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"postman\",\n  \"agent_id\": \"postman\",\n  \"product_id\": \"{{product_id}}\",\n  \"variant\": \"\",\n  \"expected_total\": \"{{expected_total}}\",\n  \"budget_cap\": \"{{budget_cap}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) pm.environment.set('pending_order_id', pm.response.json().pending_order_id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Confirm purchase (explicit confirmation)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_base_url}}/purchase/confirm"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
